.DS_Store
.env
*.env
*.pem
*.key
*.log
# Public-capable repo: factory-internal artefacts live in object-lesson-private and are
# never tracked here. Ignored as a backstop — scaffolding does not create them in this
# tree, so these entries should never match anything. If they start matching, something
# reintroduced the leak this split exists to prevent.
mind-palace/
.control-tower/
.hekton/agent-run-log.yaml
.hekton/change-log.yaml
.hekton/build-tasks/
docs/walkthroughs/
docs/session-log.md
docs/human-understanding-check.md
docs/depth-decision.md
docs/local-assumptions.md
docs/blog-signals.md
docs/gremlin-radar.md
scripts/sync-mirror-to-vault.sh
# check-mirror-drift.sh and setup-hooks.sh deliberately NOT ignored here (deviation from
# the scaffold-project.sh template default, see docs/decisions.md 2026-08-17): the
# scaffold script's own git-init step only ever installs the pre-push hook from
# $REPO_DIR/scripts/, so leaving these two private-sibling-only would mean the hook never
# installs for any public-capable project. Both scripts are generic (no vault paths, no
# secrets) and are tracked here so the pre-push hook this repo relies on actually works.
__pycache__/
node_modules/
.venv/
dist/
build/
*.bak.*
.project-setup/
# Astro's generated content-collection cache (site/.astro/): regenerated on every
# build/dev/check, not source. Matches borrow-native's/terminal-velocity's site/.gitignore
# convention.
.astro/

# Vault-wiring scripts: never ship, but must stay on disk.
#
# The accepted open-core boundary spec grades scripts/check-mirror-drift.sh and
# scripts/setup-hooks.sh as HOLD — they wire a repo to the private mind-palace
# mirror and are meaningless (and instance-coupling) to anyone cloning this.
#
# They are NOT deleted, because docs/decisions.md (2026-08-17) deliberately placed
# them here: scaffold-project.sh's git-init step only ever looks for
# scripts/setup-hooks.sh inside the public repo, so the pre-push hook installs
# nowhere else. That hook tests `-x scripts/check-mirror-drift.sh` at run time, so
# untracking the files preserves the decision's intent — the hook still works
# locally — while stopping them from being published.
scripts/check-mirror-drift.sh
scripts/setup-hooks.sh
